{{Use dmy dates|date=May 2018}}
'''Group 4 of the [[1950 FIFA World Cup]]''' took place on 2 July 1950. The group consisted of [[Uruguay national football team|Uruguay]], [[France national football team|France]], and [[Bolivia national football team|Bolivia]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.fifa.com/worldcup/news/y=2013/m=12/news=brazil-first-world-cup-draw-2238709.html |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140614002515/http://www.fifa.com/worldcup/news/y=2013/m=12/news=brazil-first-world-cup-draw-2238709.html |url-status=dead |archive-date=14 June 2014 |title=Brazil's first World Cup draw |date=3 December 2013 |publisher=FIFA}}</ref> However, France later withdrew from the group. The group winners advanced to the [[1950 FIFA World Cup#Final round|final round]].

